	/*
	* Every container the engine hands us has its buffer from FMemory, which is FMallocBinned sitting
	* on its own pools - not the CRT heap. Allocating one of these buffers with malloc, or releasing
	* an engine buffer with free, hands a pointer to an allocator that never owned it. That does not
	* fault where it happens: it corrupts a free list and the process dies later somewhere unrelated.
	* So everything in this file that owns memory goes through here.
	*
	* Realloc is the only entry point the engine exports for this, and the other two are the shapes
	* it already understands - a null Original allocates, a zero Count frees. Defined in SDK/Basic.cpp,
	* because resolving it needs the image base and this header is included before that is declared.
	*/
